From 781ee4ae033faab7dfe56934a0dc27a5ca7fef67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:28:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] yuzu_cmd: --window-rect and --aux-rect for a fixed two-window
 layout

Add --window-rect x,y,w,h (main window) and --aux-rect x,y,w,h (aux
window) so one virtual display can hold both windows at known places,
e.g. --window-rect 0,0,1920,1080 --aux-rect 0,1080,1240,1080 on a
1920x2160 display.

With a rect the window is created SDL_WINDOW_BORDERLESS instead of
SDL_WINDOW_RESIZABLE (on Windows SDL gives a resizable window
WS_THICKFRAME | WS_MAXIMIZEBOX, which a capture host may stretch to
fill the display) and is then moved and sized with
SDL_SetWindowPosition/SDL_SetWindowSize. The aux window also gets
SDL_WINDOW_NOT_FOCUSABLE (WS_EX_NOACTIVATE on Windows), so a tap on it
never takes focus from the game window. Without the flags every
SDL_CreateWindow call passes the same flags as before.

The value parser is std-only (src/yuzu_cmd/window_rect.{h,cpp}) so it
can be tested without SDL or the emulator; a bad value prints its
reason and eden-cli exits with failure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
